[require map::box::table-display [opt [vset VERSION]]]
[description]

This package provides a widget showing the information of many [term geo/box] definitions in a
table.

[para] The widget takes the boxes to show from a store, see section [sectref Store]. Each row of the table
shows a row number, followed by the name, the latitude and longitude of the center, the diameter, and the perimeter of the box. Distances are formatted for display with [cmd {map slippy pretty-distance}] of
package [package map::slippy]. The table has the columns [const #], [const Name], [const Lat], [const Lon], [const Diameter], and [const Perimeter].

[para] A box with several names is shown in several rows, one per name. A box without names is
shown in a single row with an empty name.

[para] Clicking on a column label sorts the table by that column, clicking again reverses the
order. A click with the [const Shift] key held adds the column to the sort columns.

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ::map::box::table-display] [arg pathName] [arg store] [opt [arg options]...]]

Creates a new table widget [arg pathName] showing the boxes held by [arg store], and configures it
with the specified options. The result of the command is [arg pathName]. The command is also
available as [cmd {map box table-display}].

[para] [arg store] is a command prefix for the store, see section [sectref Store].

[para] The widget supports the following option:

[list_begin options]
[opt_def -on-selection [arg cmdprefix]]

A command prefix which is invoked when the user selects a row of the table. It is invoked at idle
time, at the global level, with one additional argument, the id of the box shown in the selected
row. The result of the command is ignored.

[para] Selections made through method [method focus] are not reported.

[para] The default is the empty string, i.e. selections are not reported.

[list_end]
[list_end]

The widget supports the standard methods [method cget] and [method configure], and the
following method:

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg pathName] [method focus] [arg id]]

Selects all rows showing the box with the specified [arg id], and scrolls the table to make
them visible. It is an error if the table does not show the box [arg id].

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[list_end]

[section Store]

The widget reads the boxes to show from [arg store] once, about 100 milliseconds after its
creation. Later changes in the store are not shown.

[para] The widget uses the following methods of the store, invoked at the global level by
appending them to the [arg store] command prefix. They are a subset of the store API described in
[package map::box::store::memory].

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg store] [method ids]]

Returns a list of the ids of all boxes in the store.

[call [arg store] [method get] [arg id]]

Returns a dictionary describing the box with the specified [arg id]. The widget uses the following
keys of the dictionary, and ignores any others:

[list_begin definitions]
[def [const names]] A list of the names of the box.
[def [const center]] The center of the box, a latitude/longitude pair.
[def [const diameter]] The diameter of the box, in meters.
[def [const perimeter]] The perimeter of the box, in meters.
[list_end]

[package map::box::store::memory] provides these.

[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

[example {
package require map::box::store::fs
package require map::box::store::memory
package require map::box::table-display

map box store fs     boxes-fs /path/to/directory/of/box/files
map box store memory boxes    boxes-fs
map box table-display .boxes boxes -on-selection {apply {{id} {
    puts "selected box $id"
}}}
pack .boxes -fill both -expand 1
}]

